+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling Stays Out
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 was confirmed a deliberate non-goal on 2026-08-08: a booked visit was immutable, neither changed nor cancelled. [That ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) recorded that narrowing the row later requires a separate recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+The owner has now made that decision (2026-08-28). Correcting a booked visit's date and description is wanted: the same forward-only correction the sample already demonstrates for owner and pet details, now extended to a visit. Cancelling a booked visit was considered alongside and held out.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner wants a visit's date and description correctable, matching the forward-only correction owner and pet records already carry.
+2. **Narrow NG-5 to cover correction and cancellation.** Rejected: cancellation is removal, which sits with NG-4's deletion boundary and adds nothing the sample needs to teach.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to correction only** (chosen). Correcting a booked visit is in scope; cancelling stays out.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 is narrowed. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, realized by REQ-VIS-003, and validated exactly as booking is. Cancelling a booked visit remains a deliberate non-goal under NG-5. The sample keeps its forward-only correction shape — records are corrected, never removed.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-5 now declines only cancellation of a booked visit; correction is a requirement.
+- The sample demonstrates forward-only correction across all three record kinds — owner, pet, and visit.
+- No cancel or delete flow for a visit is planned; reopening that part of NG-5 would be its own recorded owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row and preamble.
+- [PRD Visits, REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the visit-correction requirement this narrowing admits.
